      "side": 1,
      "message": "This CL also rewrites av1_write_coeffs_txb(): the inline eob \u003d\u003d 1 path\nand the noinline write_coeffs_txb_multi(). The commit message doesn\u0027t\nmention that part, and it overlaps with my change\nhttps://aomedia-review.googlesource.com/c/aom/+/219321, which reworks\nthe same function in a different way.\n\nWith the split, every symbol still goes through aom_write_symbol().\nEach call loads low, rng and cnt from od_ec_enc, branches on the\nsymbol, renormalizes and stores the state back. The next symbol needs\nthat state, so the store and the reload sit on the critical path.\n\n219321 takes the coder state once per transform block and keeps it in\nregisters from the eob symbol to the last sign. The symbol coder\ncomputes both ends of the range and picks one, so it doesn\u0027t branch on\nthe symbol value. The sign loop walks a list of nonzero coefficients\nbuilt without branches, so it doesn\u0027t mispredict on coefficient data\neither. The output is bit exact.\n\nThe two don\u0027t combine well. A noinline helper forces the state back to\nmemory before the call and a reload after it, and the eob \u003d\u003d 1 path\nwould need its own copy of the state handling.\n\nCould you drop the av1_write_coeffs_txb() change from this CL? I think\nthat\u0027s the better option, since 219321 already replaces the same code.\nIf you want to keep it, please move it into a separate CL. Then we can\ncompare it with 219321 directly, and the rest of 219203 isn\u0027t blocked.",
